## Vegetation
Typical behavior:
high NIR reflectance
moderate green
specific texture

## Snow
Typical behavior:
bright visible bands
unique SWIR behavior

## Water
Typical behavior:
absorbs NIR
dark spectral response

## Rocky Terrain
Typical behavior:
irregular textures
mixed reflectance


## THESE MODEL NEVER UNDERSTAND IF IT IS A MOUNTAIN OR PLAIN FEILD OR WATER IT UNDERSTAND "mathematical patterns associated with terrain types"

Step 1 - Input tile enters network
Step 2 - Prediction generated
Step 3 - Prediction compared with pseudo-labels.
Pseudo-labels derived from:
NDVI
NDSI
NDWI
Step 4 - Loss function computes error
Step 5 - Backpropagation updates weights.
Over Many Epochs
The model gradually learns:
terrain semantics
vegetation structures
snow boundaries
spectral relationships

## MultiSSL = general Earth-image understanding
## U-Net = pixel-wise terrain segmentation
## KAN = complex nonlinear environmental relationships